LOK: links update when the client asks, each failure named

LOK loads without an update mode, so Calc and Writer never read a
linked source; the only way to update was the "Allow updating" bar,
which LOK has none of. Ely shows the saved values and offers the
update (LOK-11).
- .uno:ElyUpdateLinks allows link updates for the document and reads
  every link again; the answer lists the sources not read; no dialog.
  Calc: a linked sheet or area is read only when its file loads and
  holds every sheet or range it copies; otherwise it is named and its
  saved cells stay (Calc would overwrite them with "The link could not
  be updated" or nothing). ScAreaLink::FindExtRange is public for this.
  A whole-CSV area (CSV_all) is read only when the CSV has cells.
  A DDE or WEBSERVICE link that fails is named;
  sources no formula has read yet are linked first, then the external
  references read. Calc's own "Allow updating" path is unchanged.
  Writer updates each link of the link manager.
- Under LOK, Calc's refresh timers (a link's "Update every n seconds")
  never start: only the client's request reads linked data, so an
  unread source is not overwritten later and a later save waits.
  The interval itself is kept and saved.
- Writer skips a file link whose file is missing: a linked section
  would empty itself and keep nothing.
- Calc read a source from any open document of that URL, the hidden
  copy another book loaded for its own link included: an update then
  showed that copy's old values. Such copies are skipped.
- .uno:ExternalLinks in Writer lists the files and DDE servers the
  links read. Calc's lists the file it reads: a relative link
  follows the book.

